meta {
  name: tag: xyops (stats)
  type: http
  seq: 25
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/pods/templates/xyops/tags
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  X-Tapis-Token: {{X-Tapis-Token}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "kind": "pod",
    "pod_definition": {
      "image": "pixlcore/xyops:latest",
      "description": "xyOps server - built-in quick_monitors track host CPU/mem/disk stats out of the box. SECRET_KEY is a stable per-pod random so encrypted data survives restarts; /opt/xyops/data is ephemeral (use a tapisvolume for durable history).",
      "time_to_stop_default": -1,
      "environment_variables": {
        "XYOPS_secret_key": "${pods:secrets:XYOPS_SECRET_KEY}"
      },
      "secret_map": {
        "XYOPS_SECRET_KEY": "${pods:random:32}"
      },
      "volume_mounts": {
        "/opt/xyops/data": {
          "type": "ephemeral",
          "read_only": false
        }
      },
      "networking": {
        "default": {
          "protocol": "http",
          "port": 5522,
          "tapis_auth": true,
          "tapis_auth_allowed_users": [
            "*"
          ],
          "tapis_auth_return_path": "/"
        }
      },
      "healthchecks": {
        "readiness": {
          "http_get_path": "/",
          "http_get_port": 5522,
          "initial_delay_seconds": 15,
          "period_seconds": 10
        },
        "liveness": {
          "http_get_path": "/",
          "http_get_port": 5522,
          "initial_delay_seconds": 45,
          "period_seconds": 15
        },
        "networking_requires_ready": true
      },
      "resources": {
        "cpu_request": 500,
        "cpu_limit": 2000,
        "mem_request": 512,
        "mem_limit": 2048
      }
    },
    "tag": "stats",
    "commit_message": "xyOps server - built-in quick_monitors (host stats), stable secret_key, ephemeral data.",
    "description": "Simple xyOps tag: a running server that monitors host CPU/mem/disk via built-in quick_monitors. Add your own HTTP/uptime monitors in the UI."
  }
}

docs {
  ## xyOps — `stats` (simple)
  
  A bare, working xyOps server. Because xyOps ships **built-in `quick_monitors`** (host CPU / memory
  / disk), this tag is monitoring server stats the moment it's up — the analog of gatus's "green out
  of the box" example.
  
  ### How it's configured (no config file)
  xyOps uses the pixl-server framework: settings come from `XYOPS_<key>` **environment overrides**, so
  there's nothing to mount. `XYOPS_secret_key` is set to a **stable per-pod random** (`${pods:random:32}`)
  so encrypted storage stays readable across restarts.
  
  ### ⚠️ Unlike gatus, monitors/workflows are NOT declarative
  xyOps stores events/monitors/workflows in its **SQLite store under `/opt/xyops/data`** — they are
  created in the **web UI or via the API**, not embedded in config. So this tag can't "seed" a monitor
  the way the gatus config.yaml does. What you get: a running server + built-in host stats. Add a
  simple HTTP check in the UI: **Monitors → add → URL monitor** (or a "Shell" event running `curl -fsS
  https://example.com`), 1–5 min interval.
  
  ### Access / first login
  Web UI on `:5522` behind tapis_auth. xyOps initializes its store on first boot (default admin per the
  app's setup — see docs.xyops.io). If links/redirects look wrong through the proxy, set
  `XYOPS_base_app_url=https://<pod_id>.pods.<tenant-base>` (override at instantiation).
  
  ### Durability
  `/opt/xyops/data` is **ephemeral** (wiped on restart). For durable monitors/history, mount a volume:
  ```json
  "volume_mounts": { "/opt/xyops/data": { "type": "tapisvolume", "source_id": "${:?Tapis volume for xyOps data}" } }
  ```
}
